Honestly, I don't remember.

276
00:17:10,104 --> 00:17:10,584
Hmm.

277
00:17:11,484 --> 00:17:12,804
I don't know what happened.

278
00:17:13,384 --> 00:17:14,804
Or how I pulled it off.

279
00:17:15,544 --> 00:17:17,664
And remember, a man is but a thinking reed.

280
00:17:18,284 --> 00:17:19,164
Oh, wait.

281
00:17:19,404 --> 00:17:19,944
Hold on.

282
00:17:20,504 --> 00:17:21,944
I'm not saying I zoned out.

283
00:17:22,244 --> 00:17:23,124
I was thinking.

284
00:17:23,604 --> 00:17:24,404
Or trying to.

285
00:17:24,404 --> 00:17:27,184
I remember thinking I should go to the left.

286
00:17:27,404 --> 00:17:29,424
But I don't remember exactly why.

287
00:17:29,624 --> 00:17:30,784
Was there something you saw?

288
00:17:32,024 --> 00:17:32,944
I don't know.

289
00:17:33,684 --> 00:17:34,384
I guess.

290
00:17:34,904 --> 00:17:37,964
I saw Otomo running toward the goal out of the corner of my eye.

291
00:17:37,964 --> 00:17:42,544
And I felt like he knew exactly what I was trying to do.

292
00:17:42,544 --> 00:17:45,804
Even though I still didn't have a clue at that point.

293
00:17:45,804 --> 00:17:52,004
And then, I think, I closed in on the goal, just in case he missed.

294
00:17:55,084 --> 00:17:55,644
Excellent.

295
00:17:55,764 --> 00:17:56,864
He can verbalize it.

296
00:17:57,624 --> 00:17:59,024
What else did you think about?

297
00:17:59,024 --> 00:18:02,084
My mom and brother.

298
00:18:02,784 --> 00:18:03,004
Huh?

299
00:18:03,924 --> 00:18:05,684
It was my mom and my brother.

300
00:18:06,144 --> 00:18:07,164
They kept me going.

301
00:18:07,824 --> 00:18:10,484
The only reason I could score was because of them.

302
00:18:12,604 --> 00:18:16,584
Up until today, I've only ever played soccer the way I wanted to.

303
00:18:17,164 --> 00:18:21,644
I wanted to go pro, but I never considered what that actually means.

304
00:18:23,284 --> 00:18:25,204
All I've done is cause trouble.

305
00:18:25,804 --> 00:18:27,484
I owe them so much.

306
00:18:27,484 --> 00:18:29,544
I have to pay them back for it.

307
00:18:29,964 --> 00:18:32,484
The only way for me to do that is through soccer.

308
00:18:32,904 --> 00:18:33,824
By going pro.

309
00:18:34,684 --> 00:18:39,464
And, I realized how hard it would be after seeing all those guys so determined to make it.

310
00:18:40,804 --> 00:18:42,664
Thanks for bringing me out here, old man.

311
00:18:43,184 --> 00:18:45,144
No matter what happens, I'm grateful.

312
00:18:46,224 --> 00:18:48,864
I know now that even if I don't make your team,

313
00:18:49,504 --> 00:18:50,684
I'm gonna go pro.

314
00:18:51,304 --> 00:18:52,484
Because I'm meant to.

315
00:18:57,484 --> 00:19:04,524
Man, Hashito, you're something special.

316
00:19:05,104 --> 00:19:08,024
You're the only candidate who actually scored against the youth team.

317
00:19:08,264 --> 00:19:09,204
Ha, ha, ha.

318
00:19:09,564 --> 00:19:11,344
I guess I did do that, didn't I?

319
00:19:12,124 --> 00:19:12,604
See?

320
00:19:12,784 --> 00:19:13,644
What did I tell you?

321
00:19:13,644 --> 00:19:14,844
I'm totally getting signed.

322
00:19:14,844 --> 00:19:16,684
I'm a freaking genius after all.

323
00:19:16,784 --> 00:19:17,544
Ha, ha, ha.

324
00:19:17,804 --> 00:19:19,484
So if you don't hear from them at all then,

325
00:19:19,604 --> 00:19:21,564
you should just assume you didn't make it, right?

326
00:19:22,204 --> 00:19:22,464
Home.

327
00:19:23,004 --> 00:19:23,164
Hmm?

328
00:19:24,744 --> 00:19:25,144
Home.

329
00:19:25,844 --> 00:19:28,684
They did say it could take up to three weeks for them to decide.

330
00:19:29,404 --> 00:19:30,544
You've still got some time.

331
00:19:30,544 --> 00:19:36,024
And if you get in, then what?

332
00:19:36,604 --> 00:19:37,404
Do you have a plan?

333
00:19:38,204 --> 00:19:39,424
Are you ready to move to Tokyo?

334
00:19:41,424 --> 00:19:41,784
Hmm?

335
00:19:41,884 --> 00:19:42,364
All right.

336
00:19:42,684 --> 00:19:43,944
I'll see you later, Shun.

337
00:19:44,004 --> 00:19:46,404
I'm gonna head home and take a nap before my night shift.

338
00:19:46,704 --> 00:19:47,064
Cool.

339
00:19:48,064 --> 00:19:51,064
As for you, I'm giving you all a discount on the shaved ice,

340
00:19:51,164 --> 00:19:53,324
so tell your dads to come have a drink later, m'kay?

341
00:19:53,584 --> 00:19:53,844
K!

342
00:19:53,844 --> 00:20:00,004
Not a word about me taking off for the tryouts in Tokyo

343
00:20:00,004 --> 00:20:01,564
without running it by her first.

344
00:20:02,304 --> 00:20:03,824
Something's not right here.

345
00:20:04,004 --> 00:20:04,444
Ashito.

346
00:20:04,804 --> 00:20:04,984
Huh?

347
00:20:05,484 --> 00:20:07,064
I know you're pretending it doesn't matter,

348
00:20:07,204 --> 00:20:08,344
but I think it does.

349
00:20:08,664 --> 00:20:10,724
You've literally been losing sleep over it.

350
00:20:11,144 --> 00:20:11,904
Yeah, sure.

351
00:20:12,524 --> 00:20:14,424
Of course I care if I make it or not.

352
00:20:15,344 --> 00:20:16,524
But what can I do?

353
00:20:16,524 --> 00:20:19,384
I did my best and mentally prepared for the worst.

354
00:20:20,184 --> 00:20:22,724
And then I think, what if I do get in?

355
00:20:22,724 --> 00:20:25,324
There's no way I could move to Tokyo by myself.

356
00:20:25,504 --> 00:20:26,364
I'm a mess.

357
00:20:28,864 --> 00:20:29,824
Doesn't matter.

358
00:20:30,624 --> 00:20:31,724
I hope I get picked.

359
00:20:33,604 --> 00:20:34,544
I do.

360
00:20:42,464 --> 00:20:45,764
Uh, Ashito, what's that thing sticking out of your pocket?

361
00:20:46,644 --> 00:20:47,304
Is it a letter?

362
00:20:47,764 --> 00:20:48,524
Oh, this?

363
00:20:48,524 --> 00:20:53,544
I almost forgot about this one.

364
00:20:55,844 --> 00:20:57,564
Don't read it till you're back in Ehime.

365
00:20:58,444 --> 00:20:59,704
Promise me you won't!

366
00:21:00,184 --> 00:21:00,504
Uh?

367
00:21:03,244 --> 00:21:04,624
Dude, are you for real?

368
00:21:04,824 --> 00:21:06,184
From the manager's sister?

369
00:21:06,504 --> 00:21:08,384
Did she seriously write you a love letter?

370
00:21:08,484 --> 00:21:09,184
Of course not.

371
00:21:09,244 --> 00:21:09,944
Don't be an idiot.

372
00:21:10,704 --> 00:21:12,564
It doesn't make a lot of sense anyway.

373
00:21:12,564 --> 00:21:16,024
Did she write you a meal plan?

374
00:21:16,244 --> 00:21:16,544
Oh.

375
00:21:16,824 --> 00:21:18,704
Is she trying to be a nutritionist or something?

376
00:21:19,344 --> 00:21:20,004
I don't know.

377
00:21:20,184 --> 00:21:21,024
I didn't ask her.

378
00:21:21,884 --> 00:21:25,004
I mean, she did help me keep going through tryouts.

379
00:21:25,284 --> 00:21:26,884
So I'm grateful to her for that.

380
00:21:29,404 --> 00:21:32,344
Bro, you've been sitting on a valuable resource.

381
00:21:33,244 --> 00:21:33,724
Call her.

382
00:21:34,224 --> 00:21:35,504
She's the manager's sister.

383
00:21:35,924 --> 00:21:36,944
She knows if you made it.

384
00:21:36,944 --> 00:21:50,024
Hello?

385
00:21:50,844 --> 00:21:51,824
Uh, Ashito.

386
00:21:52,464 --> 00:21:52,644
Huh?

387
00:21:53,344 --> 00:21:55,024
This came in the mail for you.

388
00:22:02,124 --> 00:22:03,184
I was curious.

389
00:22:03,684 --> 00:22:05,224
I'm sorry I opened it before you.

390
00:22:05,224 --> 00:22:07,224
Congratulations.

391
00:22:07,224 --> 00:22:09,224
Congratulations.

392
00:22:19,224 --> 00:22:21,224
Great, right?

393
00:22:21,224 --> 00:22:23,224
I'm proud of you.

394
00:22:23,224 --> 00:22:25,224
But I'm torn about soccer.

395
00:22:25,224 --> 00:22:27,224
It's taking you away from me.

396
00:22:35,224 --> 00:22:37,224
I'm proud of you.

397
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:27,606
Next time on Aowashi Orange Scenery.

